## Hints for Future Agents
- --copilot is opt-in on purpose: auto-rebase.sh runs `gpo.sh -f` on every rebase and must never trigger paid reviews.
- The happy path (`gh pr edit N --add-reviewer @copilot` on an OPEN PR) was not executed in this session because it posts to a real work PR and consumes credits. The user runs it on the next push to PR 121. Check that the resulting review body says "Review effort level: Balanced".
- `set -x` is scoped to a subshell around git push so the gh and jq calls stay out of the trace.
- `gh pr view` exit 1 with stderr `no pull requests found for branch "X"` is the "not a PR branch" signal; its stderr is intentionally left visible.

## Codebase Discoveries
- gh 2.101.0 maps @copilot to bot login copilot-pull-request-reviewer (CopilotReviewerLogin in api/queries_repo.go) and uses the requestReviewsByLogin mutation with botLogins ["copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]"].
- Effort level (Lite/Balanced) lives in Settings > Copilot > Code review at repo or org level. Rulesets only toggle automatic requests, review-on-push, and draft review.
- This repo's post-commit hook (git-autopush-post-commit) pushes master on every commit.

